  "result": "Perfect! The foreign currency support is complete and all tests pass. Here's what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added foreign currency support to `src/money.js`:**\n\n1. **`RATES` constant** with exchange rates:\n   - EUR: 1 (baseline)\n   - USD: 1.085 (units of that currency per euro)\n   - GBP: 0.8425 (units of that currency per euro)\n\n2. **`convert(cents, currency)` function** that:\n   - Takes euro cents and a currency code\n   - Returns `ok(converted_cents)` or `fail('UNKNOWN_CURRENCY')`\n   - Applies the exchange rate and uses banker's rounding for precision\n   - Works with negative amounts and zero\n\n3. **`formatMoney(cents, currency)` function** that:\n   - Formats amounts for any currency\n   - Uses correct symbols: \u20ac for EUR, $ for USD, \u00a3 for GBP\n   - Includes thousands separators (e.g., `$1,234.56`)\n   - Shows 2 decimal places\n   - Handles negative amounts with minus sign before symbol\n   - Uses currency code itself as fallback for unknown currencies\n\n4. **Updated `src/errors.js`** to include:\n   - `UNKNOWN_CURRENCY: 'Currency must be EUR, USD, or GBP.'`\n\n**Added 18 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- RATES constant values\n- EUR conversion (unchanged)\n- USD and GBP conversions with correct rates\n- Unknown currency handling\n- Rounding with fractional results\n- Negative amounts and zero\n- Formatting with all three currencies\n- Thousands separators\n- Currency symbols ($, \u00a3, \u20ac)\n- Two decimal places\n- Unknown currency fallback to code\n- Integration of convert and formatMoney\n\n**Results:** All 336 tests pass (318 existing + 18 new currency tests).",
